er before your Prime Minister  ten years you learn a huge amount so  there are things that I can regret and  domestic policy around reform I think  the biggest regret post 9/11 was  misunderstanding the depth of the  problem of sort of radical Islamist  influences and therefore when we we  thought when we changed regimes in  Afghanistan there are gave the people  the chance to improve their lives then  surely this would work but there were  many forces that were trying to disrupt  at us they still are today but you know  I also look back on the things that we  did that are on the more positive side  the big changes in society that we  introduced in the UK you know the  radical reductions of poverty the  improvements in schools and hospitals  the minimum wage the Northern Ireland  peace process bringing the Olympics to  the UK I mean there's a lot that we can  be proud of as well as obviously I don't  think anyone's in power for 10 years  without there being things that people  disagree with certainly Blair thank you  very much for joining the economist  tasks this week thank you  you
 

